<%# Flash banner for public, customer-facing pages, rendered once from the
    shared application layout so every public page shows notices. Owner
    pages have their own equivalent at owner/shared/_flash, rendered from
    the separate owner layout. The wrapping container only appears when
    there is something to show, so a flash-less page gets no extra
    whitespace at the top.

    Each state is a ruled band, not a card: the daisyUI colour variant
    supplies the ground, and a mono label plus its own icon name the state
    in words as well, so success and error never rest on colour alone.
    `role="alert"` announces the band without moving focus into it.

    Width/alignment default to max-w-2xl, matching the menu/cart/status
    pages this was built for. A page laid out narrower than that (the
    centred auth pages) sets content_for(:flash_class) above its own
    content to keep the banner from rendering wider than the form it
    refers to — see sessions/new and registrations/new. %>
<% if notice || alert %>
  <%# w-full is load-bearing and belongs here rather than on the band: this div
      is a flex item of the column-flex <body>, and the `mx-auto` in every
      flash_class cancels the default stretch, so without it this wrapper
      shrinks to its own text and the full-width band inside it follows.
      The band's own width comes from the `.alert` reskin in the stylesheet. %>
  <div class="w-full <%= content_for(:flash_class).presence || "max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4" %> pt-6">
    <% if notice %>
      <div role="alert" class="alert alert-success flex items-start gap-3 mb-6">
        <%= icon "check-circle", css: "size-4 shrink-0 mt-1" %>
        <span class="mono-label shrink-0"><%= t("shared.flash_notice") %></span>
        <span class="min-w-0"><%= notice %></span>
      </div>
    <% end %>
    <% if alert %>
      <div role="alert" class="alert alert-error flex items-start gap-3 mb-6">
        <%= icon "warning", css: "size-4 shrink-0 mt-1" %>
        <span class="mono-label shrink-0"><%= t("shared.flash_error") %></span>
        <span class="min-w-0"><%= alert %></span>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
